WEBVTT

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.740
<i>Everyone has a wish...</i>

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.700
<i>...that they hope to have granted.</i>

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.720
<i>If it means having that wish granted...</i>

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.350
<i>...you wouldn't think twice about
diving into a grueling battle.</i>

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:13.010
Where am I?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.910
The King is seeking a new living sacrifice.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.060
Huh, we starting up again?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.490
A Rebuild notification?

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.000
Declare your participation
by nightfall a week from today.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.500
If you don't make it in time...

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.710
I'm going to find it, no matter what.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.190
Come back here!

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.570
Give it up already!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.150
Damn you, you're mocking me.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.200
How'd you get up there?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.450
Enough already!

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.710
Huh, that's all you get if you don't use it in battle?

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.500
Still, I did capture you.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.380
Huh?

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.340
So you were using a counter?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.590
Hey, come back here!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.320
Huh? Who the hell are you?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.320
Listen, would you mind backing off?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:41.030
Shut up! You're the one who came up to me.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.700
Just shut your mouth and hand over that key chip.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.330
You're not good enough to survive this battle.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.620
What? Anyway, that match didn't count.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.700
Hey!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.960
That was just a bad draw. Huh?

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.670
What's your problem?

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:55.790
The bread...

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.420
Huh?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.380
The bread is crying.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.630
Huh?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.850
What kind of garbage are you spewing?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.520
Huh?

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.360
Excuse me...

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.660
I'll buy you another one.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.120
Do you forgive me now?

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.540
Oh, you're still here?

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.710
I can see that you're a formidable player.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:43.220
I'm not really sure what this card is.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.510
Before I knew it, it was in my hand.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.140
What?

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.640
You only just got here?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.060
Let me give you a rundown.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.190
This is Build-Divide.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:06.200
It's what you need to live in this city,
which is ruled by the King.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:11.080
It's also what you need to have your wish granted.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.540
Wish?

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.290
Do you have a minute?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:23.300
All right. Dealer!

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.720
Request battle.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.930
Deploying defensive barrier.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.770
What's this, magic?

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.730
It's a shield that'll let us battle safely.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.820
So you set me up?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.200
I want you to show me how good you are.

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.700
Then explain.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.370
We're going to have a card battle now.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.660
I'll explain how it works as we go along.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.420
These cards with this mysterious
power are Build-Divide.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:04.630
There's a forty-card deck,
and a single Territory Card.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.970
You use forty-one cards to battle.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.380
Territory...

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.100
When your own Ace Card shows up,
the card that flips over like this...

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.720
...this Territory Card is the key to victory.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.560
Okay, once your scan is complete,
activate your scout lens.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.900
Now blink twice in a row.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.690
You can leave the rest to visual augmentation.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.280
Your cards too. Like this!

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.450
Last but not least...

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.580
Call. Iora!

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.800
Now, you do it too.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:49.970
Call.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.600
A Bloom card, I see.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.560
Bloom...

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.110
All right, ready to get started?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:11.280
Oh, my name is Sakura Banka. What's yours?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.200
Teruto Kurabe.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:15.080
Teruto Kurabe?

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.160
I've heard that name before.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.410
Teruto Kurabe will make the first move.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.000
Teruto versus Sakura. Ready?

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.040
Build-Divide!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.420
Your turn first, okay?

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.630
Start by placing one card in the Energy Zone.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:34.260
Along with the Energy that was already there,
you'll be able to use three Energy.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.350
Next pick a card from your hand.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:40.560
The number at the top left shows
the color and Cost you'll need.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.230
Does the color match the Energy?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:43.980
Yeah.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.440
Then use the Energy and play your cards.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:50.610
First rest your cards by placing them sideways.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.200
When you release a unit, remember
to announce it by saying, "Accept."

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.200
Accept.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.490
Nadiya, Brahmadatta.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.580
Using Nadiya's ability to draw
one card from the deck.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.590
If you're out of Energy, you basically
can't play your cards anymore.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.340
Next, Attack Phase.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:11.720
Units that appear in the field
can launch an immediate attack.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:17.300
Right now, since there's nothing in my field,
rest your cards and try attacking the player directly.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.470
Nadiya, attack the player.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.150
Trigger check.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.520
No trigger. Send your Life Card to the Cemetery.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.780
You're finishing with one damage.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:35.490
When this life falls to zero,
and you sustain one more damage, you lose.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.580
If you have nothing else planned to do,
your turn is over.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:39.410
Right.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.750
Okay, now it's my turn. Draw.

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.750
Energy Set. I'll use three Energy.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.210
Accept. Rabbian, Moonlight.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.550
You can target cards at rest.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:56.680
Rabbian, attack Nadiya!

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:03.770
When units battle each other, they inflict
damage on each other according to their power.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.060
Does that give you an idea of how it all works?

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.480
All right, now it's your turn.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:09.770
Draw.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.690
I'll use three Energy, and Accept.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.780
Partial Dealer.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.740
Attack Rabbian.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:21.990
Looks like you're getting the hang of it.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:27.370
But when Rabbian heads to the Cemetery,
she leaves the top of her life in the Energy Zone.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.340
If you're done, I'm going to take my turn, okay?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:31.340
Right.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:35.550
Okay, thanks to Rabbian, I have all five Energy.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.300
So let me show you what the
world of Build-Divide is really like.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:40.640
Use all five Energy.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:44.060
Annihilate everything in your path.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.640
Accept.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:49.690
TX-07 Dio Sirius. Iora!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.370
Territory.

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.170
Build Arise!

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.930
Heavy Artillery Base...

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.300
...Vulbabylon!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.560
Well? Mind-blowing isn't it?

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.560
This is my Territory.

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:35.320
In this Build-Divide, whoever uses Open Territory
and maximizes their unit's ability will win.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:40.490
Invoking Iora's ability, Scout Three.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:45.870
I'm going to look at the top three cards in my deck,
and move them to the bottom of my deck.

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.580
I'm using Iora to attack Partial Dealer.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.540
Invoking Attack Effect.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.170
Sending the topmost card in my deck that
I switched out with Scout to the Cemetery.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:59.130
If it's a Command Card less than three Cost,
I can play it without paying the Cost.

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:01.550
Command. New Weapon Development.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.930
Now I’ll invoke Vulbabylon's Territory powers.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.310
If I play a Command Card worth less than five Cost,

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.690
I can remove one card from my deck and copy it.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:13.230
First, I'll draw two cards for the two I copied.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.400
Next, I'll draw two cards for the two originals.

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:16.650
Attack with Iora!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:17.480
Launch!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.160
End of turn. Well?

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.620
Do you see how important Open Territory is?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.250
<i>Territory.</i>

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:41.970
What was that?

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:44.140
Something wrong?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.260
No. Now it's my turn.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:48.140
Accept.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.600
Viena, Battle Engineer.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.020
Invoking Viena's ability.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.110
I'm drawing one card from my deck,

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.610
and taking my deck's Cap—

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:01.490
Removing Rizome from my deck.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:03.570
My turn.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.660
Accepting Tranlock.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.160
Announcing a player attack by Iora.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.290
Invoking Attack Effect.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.370
Sending the topmost card
in my deck to the Cemetery.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:15.830
Three cost. Playing the Surprise Attack command.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.290
Resting Viena.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.210
Then you can't block me.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.630
Now, attack with Iora!

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.060
Use Tranlock for a Two-Hit Attack on the player.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:36.560
First card, no trigger.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:38.480
One more card with the second hit.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:39.980
What's this?

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.570
Check your Life Cards.

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:45.410
The skull mark is a Burst Trigger.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:49.160
Sorry, but I'm going to have you
sustain additional damage.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:54.670
There are always twelve of those
Buster Cards with that mark.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:59.250
So if you're out of luck and your
remaining lives are all Burst Triggers...

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.050
All right, check to see how much life
you have after Burst Trigger damage.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.770
One more card with the second hit.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:17.900
But you've lost a whopping
four lives just in that turn.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.900
At this rate, it'll be over for you in a flash.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.240
Are you trying to lose?

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.070
Who are you?

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:28.320
You know there's someone you need to defeat.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:35.960
Defeat him.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:40.710
Defeat him! Defeat him! Defeat him!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.460
Defeat the King!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:44.220
King.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.800
That's right.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:50.050
I've got to defeat him.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.310
The King...

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.690
Sorry to keep you waiting, Bloom.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.110
Let's get started.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.700
My turn.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.370
This is the path...

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.080
...that I must take.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:20.330
Sending all living beings into chaos.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.420
Repeating death and rebirth.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:25.550
Accept!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.760
Bloom, Soul Wager!

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.650
Territory. Build Arise.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.120
Casino of Fate.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.460
Invoking the ability of the
Territory, Casino of Fate.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.380
Sending the top two cards from
my deck to the Cemetery.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:11.090
Of these two cards, the effect will be determined
based on how many Buster Cards there are.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.930
They're both Buster Cards.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:17.220
Destroying all units except for Bloom.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:22.190
Now I'm resting Bloom and activating her ability.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.690
Removing six cards from the Cemetery,

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.740
and sending units worth less than
the total Cost of number of Energy,

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:28.860
from the Cemetery to the field.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.530
That card's the one you dropped into the Cemetery.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.700
Revive.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.660
Rizome, Black Knight!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.170
Rizome, attack the player.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:51.260
You were lucky there was no trigger.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:52.970
End of turn.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:57.680
What's going on? This wasn't your first time?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:01.350
Also you said, "I've got to defeat the King."

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:06.440
Teruto Kurabe. Who are you exactly?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.950
#01 When You Wish Upon a Star

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.030
Attacking with Zophia!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.700
Attacking with Rizome!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:23.920
My turn.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.630
Command, Capital Breaker.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:30.130
Removing one card from my hand,
and using my Territory ability to copy it.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.590
Inflicting eight thousand damage to each unit.

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.760
Both blasts to target Rizome!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.640
What? Is something wrong?

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:45.230
No. I'm starting to enjoy this a little.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.360
Listen, do you want to defeat the King too?

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.780
I wonder if you know how to defeat him.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.740
I could tell you, you know.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.910
That is, if you can beat me in this battle, okay?

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:05.500
Right now, you have two lives left,
and your only unit is Bloom.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:10.340
I've got six lives, and in my field
I've got Two-Hit Zophia.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.880
Even so...

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:17.260
Unless I hit a Burst,
I can't win with just the Two-Hit.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.100
Besides...

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.390
I can't just ignore Bloom.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.060
Zophia!

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:31.690
All right, what are you going to do, Teruto?

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.400
If you lose a match like this,
you'll never reach the King.

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.660
King.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.950
She's right.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.580
That's who you've got to defeat.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.540
Zophia, attack Bloom!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.960
<i>The one I've got to defeat.</i>

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.500
<i>The place I've got to reach.</i>

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:49.710
<i>Me?</i>

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.920
Come on. Just keep coming.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.420
Till you make it here.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:59.550
<i>The path I've got to follow!</i>

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.520
Invoking Bloom's ability before the battle.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.230
Sending the top card to the Cemetery.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.560
A Buster Card?

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:12.320
Right. If it's a Buster Card,
I can add five thousand to Bloom's power.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.450
Zophia...

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.450
<i>I'm going. I'm taking the path to victory.</i>

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.170
Now it's my turn. Accept.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.540
Partial Dealer!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.460
Attack the player!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:35.970
No trigger. Now you attack too, Bloom!

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.840
Burst Trigger?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.600
<i>Difference in lives, two to three.</i>

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.600
My turn.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.230
Iora. I can't win with just these cards.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.520
I've got to at least take out the Partial Dealer.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.610
Accept Iora.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.480
Attack the Partial Dealer!

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.490
<i>I really wish that I could've defeated Bloom.</i>

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:05.080
<i>Bloom, a witch who can resurrect
units from their deathbeds.</i>

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.040
<i>Could it be that you're protecting Teruto...</i>

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:13.920
<i>...as well as me?</i>

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.960
My turn.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.420
All right, this is the end.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.590
Let's finish this, Bloom.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.680
Resting Bloom, and activating her ability!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.100
Removing the six cards from my Cemetery.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.810
Rise from the darkness.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.940
Riverwort, DeadRook!

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.230
Since the Territory was Open when he appeared...

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.860
I can subtract six thousand
from each of my opponent's units.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:42.570
Resurrecting Riverwort with his
Two-Hit Attack gives you a lot of firepower,

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:44.530
but I have three lives left.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:48.830
Unless there are at least two Bursts,
there's no chance for a comeback. That could—

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:49.620
It can.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:56.840
Like you explained, there are twelve cards in this
forty-card deck that can be Burst Triggers.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:00.840
The number of cards you used in this battle then,

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:04.720
in your field, Energy Zone, Cemetery, removes...

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.970
I can still only see three Buster Cards.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:12.560
You've got nine cards left.
One in your hand, three lives.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:17.400
Meaning that out of a total of thirteen cards,
nine are Buster Cards.

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.610
You remember?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:22.570
There's an eighty-percent chance that a
Burst will appear out of your remaining lives.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:26.660
I've got an eighty-percent chance of finishing this now.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.540
Even still, if no Bursts appear...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:31.910
Then I'll probably lose.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:36.340
That's why this is where the fun really starts.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.000
Riverwort!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.050
This is the path that I believe in!

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:04.660
<i>I've found him.</i>

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.620
<i>The one who will seize the stars.</i>

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.120
<i>Teruto, I'm going to...</i>

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.830
<i>...stake everything I have on you.</i>

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.880
Winner, Teruto Kurabe.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.680
I guess I lose.

00:21:29.810 --> 00:21:31.850
Hey, you like bread?

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:36.690
If you accept these, I'll treat you to tons of bread.

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:40.860
Just as I promised, the way to defeat the King.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:46.910
Rebuild, a special Build-Divide battle where
you stake your right to challenge the King.

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:52.830
Once you've collected twenty-one key chips
to complete a key, you can take on the King.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:56.750
That's how you can get your wish
granted here in Neo Kyoto.

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.330
I have no wish.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.670
Well, I do!

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.420
There's a wish that I want to have granted.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:07.010
But I'm not good enough to make it to the King.

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:10.100
Please, Teruto.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:15.230
Take me with you to the King.

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:24.940
I'm going, whether you tell me to or not.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:26.780
To the King.

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.080
Dealer! Register him.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.670
Teruto Kurabe has been registered.

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:40.880
This officially makes you a challenger to the King.

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:43.000
Good to have you aboard, Teruto.

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:46.800
There's one more thing I want you to tell me.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:48.050
What is it?

00:22:49.390 --> 00:22:52.350
Do you know where my house is?

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:53.680
Your house?

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:00.270
He has returned.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:03.860
Now then, let's get started.

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:16.450
Man, this is starting to get interesting.

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:22.960
Now then, who will be the one to reach me?

00:23:23.920 --> 00:23:25.880
What a spectacle that'll be!

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.970
TO BE CONTINUED

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:33.660
My only wish is to defeat the King. That's all.

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:35.910
You really don't remember anything, do you?

00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:39.460
Now, let's get the game started!

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.980
#02 Lonely Baby Bird
